  "question_answers": [
    {
      "question": 1,
      "answer": "OBX set id 3, probe PML_RARA: OBX-5 component 1 (cells_scored) is '2OO', written with capital letter O instead of zero, so it is not an integer. Failure INVALID_CELL_COUNT / FISH_RESULT_CONTENT / REDRIVE_ONLY; reason \"Probe PML_RARA: cells_scored '2OO' is not a valid integer.\"",
      "sources": [
        "src/interfaces/inbound_hl7.py _parse_count",
        "R-014"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": 2,
      "answer": "Filing is all-or-nothing: every OBX is validated before any result is written, and one invalid OBX routes the whole message to the error queue, so an order never holds a partially applied instrument message.",
      "sources": [
        "src/interfaces/inbound_hl7.py module docstring (ingestion contract), _validate_obx",
        "R-014"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": 3,
      "answer": "INVALID_CELL_COUNT maps to REDRIVE_ONLY (design record sec 6). An unchanged retry is approved only for ORDER_NOT_FOUND (sec 7, R-025): retrying the same payload would hit the same defect, and the service would record a REJECTED RETRY_ORIGINAL attempt. A corrected re-drive processes the supplied payload as a new message.",
      "sources": [
        "validation/v1.1-design-record.md sec 6, sec 7",
        "R-025",
        "R-027",
        "R-028"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": 4,
      "answer": "Original message 1 (control id EX03-ORIG) is still ERRORED with order_id NULL, and its payload hashes to the sha256 of the inputs/original_result.hl7 file bytes; the queue item's raw_payload hashes to the same value. The corrected payload is a distinct message 2 (control id EX03-CORR) and only it is FILED. Besides the corrected count, the corrected file differs only in MSH-7 (message time) and MSH-10 (control id).",
      "sources": [
        "validation/v1.1-design-record.md sec 4, sec 11 (I-01)",
        "R-022",
        "R-023",
        "R-028"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": 5,
      "answer": "They are equal. payload_sha256 is the SHA-256 of the exact UTF-8 payload the request processed, and the resulting message stores exactly that payload, so both equal the sha256 of inputs/corrected_result.hl7.",
      "sources": [
        "src/recovery.py _payload_sha256",
        "R-040"
      ]
    }
  ]
